# ripgrep (rg) — real-world examples

## Basic searches

```sh
# Search recursively in current directory
rg <pattern>

# Case-insensitive
rg -i <pattern>

# Whole words only
rg -w <pattern>

# Specific directory
rg <pattern> <path>
```

## Filter by file type

```sh
# Only search one file type (rg --type-list shows all)
rg <pattern> -t py

# Glob filter
rg <pattern> -g '*.conf'
```

## Output control

```sh
# File names only, no matching lines
rg -l <pattern>

# Line numbers (default when output is a terminal)
rg -n <pattern>

# Context lines before and after
rg -C 3 <pattern>

# Count matches per file
rg -c <pattern>
```

## Ignore rules

```sh
# Search hidden files AND ignored files (-uu = --hidden --no-ignore)
rg -uu <pattern>

# Don't respect .gitignore
rg --no-ignore <pattern>
```

## Homelab examples

```sh
# Where did I set that port? Search all configs as root
sudo rg -n 'ListenPort' /etc

# Find every playbook that touches the mediaserver host
rg -l 'mediaserver' ~/ansible

# Plex errors in today's logs, with context
rg -i -C 2 'error' "/var/lib/plexmediaserver/Library/Application Support/Plex Media Server/Logs" 2>/dev/null | head -40

# Which cheatsheets still lack code fences?
rg --files-without-match '```' ~/Public/ireaneus-cheatsheets
```

## Flag reference

| Flag | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `-i` | Case-insensitive |
| `-w` | Whole word match |
| `-l` | Filenames with matches only |
| `-n` | Show line numbers |
| `-c` | Count matches |
| `-C <n>` | n lines of context |
| `-t <type>` | Restrict to file type |
| `-g <glob>` | Restrict by glob |
| `-uu` | Include hidden + ignored files |
| `--no-ignore` | Ignore .gitignore rules |
